



:: day_5_1_str

The alarm buzzed beside my ear a weak, rattling thing that barely managed to pull me out of sleep. For a moment I just lay there, staring at the ceiling, feeling the heaviness from yesterday sitting like stone in my chest.

Then my eyes drifted down. The VR case rested at the foot of my bed, glowing softly in the dim room. Not accusing. Not urging. Just waiting.

<<leo "…Should I?" >>

My voice sounded as tired as I felt. I pushed myself upright, rubbing my eyes. The idea of logging in before Ava of getting a head start, of knowing what to expect it tugged at me. Hard.

But then I remembered her small voice yesterday. The way her fingers shook when she held mine. How she pressed her forehead to my chest and whispered she wanted to try… but needed me with her.

Yeah. I couldn’t go in alone. Before I could even reach for the case, my phone buzzed. Ava. Still half-asleep, I answered.

<<leo "Hey." >>

A tiny breath spilled through the speaker, fragile and warm.

<<ava "…Leo? Are you awake?" >>

Her voice felt soft enough to fold into. I shifted back against my pillow.

<<leo "Yeah. Just woke up." >>

A pause her kind of pause, the one where she folded into herself before speaking again.

<<ava "Did you… um… try the VR last night?" >>

My eyes flicked to the untouched case.

<<leo "No. I didn’t." >>

Another breath, caught halfway between relief and disbelief.

<<ava "You didn’t?" >>

<<leo "I wanted our first time in there to be together. I waited for you." >>

The line went quiet, and I could picture her sitting up in bed, covers pulled to her chin, heart squeezing behind her ribs.

<<ava "…Leo." >>

Her voice cracked.

<<ava "Can I… come over? Right now?" >>

My exhaustion evaporated.

<<leo "Yeah. Of course. Come." >>

Another tiny exhale shaky, grateful.

<<ava "Ten minutes?" >>

<<leo "I’ll unlock the door." >>

A beat. One soft heartbeat before she whispered:

<<ava "Thank you. For waiting." >>

<<leo "Always, Ava." >>

The call ended with a soft click. I sat there a moment longer, staring at the VR case glowing in the morning light, my pulse starting to climb not from fear. From knowing she was on her way.

[[Ava arrives|day_5_2_str]]


:: day_5_2_str

The hallway outside my dorm creaked faintly her footsteps, small and hesitant. I’d barely finished straightening the blankets when a soft knock tapped against my door. My chest tightened. I opened it slowly.

Ava stood there in her pale sweater, sleeves pulled over her hands, hair a little messy from rushing across campus. Her cheeks were pink from the cold… and from something warmer, something nervy. She looked up at me like she wasn’t sure she was allowed to.

<<ava "…Hi." >>

God, she looked fragile. I stepped aside.

<<leo "Come in." >>

She slipped past me, brushing lightly against my arm. Even that small touch made something in me settle. She stood in the middle of the room, staring around like being here suddenly mattered more than it ever had.

Then her eyes landed on the VR case. The soft neon glow reflecting on her face. She froze. Her fingers curled into her sleeves.

<<ava "It’s… real." >>

Her voice trembled the kind of tremble that wasn’t fear alone. Wonder, nerves, hope. I moved beside her, slow, giving her space to step away if she needed. She didn’t move.

<<leo "Hey, we’re not diving headfirst today. Just opening it together. Looking at it. That’s all." >>

She swallowed. Hard.

<<ava "I know. I just… it feels like a big step." >>

I offered my hand open, patient. I didn’t take hers. I let her choose. She stared at it for a long second. Then her small fingers slid into mine, warm and trembling. My chest loosened.

<<leo "You okay?" >>

She nodded tiny, shaky.

<<ava "I’m scared. But… I trust you." >>

Those last two words hit straight under my ribs. I squeezed her hand gently, grounding her the way she needed. Together, slowly, we walked toward the desk. The VR case glowed brighter as we approached, runes pulsing like soft breathing. Ava’s grip tightened; she leaned closer to me without even realizing she was doing it.

<<ava "So… we really open it now?" >>

<<leo "Yeah. Together." >>

She exhaled quiet, steadying herself. We reached out at the same time. My hand over hers. Her fingers shaking against mine. The lid clicked. Light bloomed and the world waited for us.

